# retroforge board catalog, read by boot/gen-bls.sh to make the board table (boards.tsv) every
# Boot Loader Specification entry is written from.
#
# Tab-separated: <device-id>\t<menu name>\t<dtb basename>\t<bootargs>
# One row per board. This is BUILD-TIME data: gen-bls.sh adds each DTB's root `model` (how the
# running system and OpenABL's Device model setting name the board) and ships the result in the
# root as /usr/lib/retroforge/boot/boards.tsv, NOT in the runtime device profiles
# (rootfs/overlay/usr/lib/retroforge/devices/*.conf, which carry no boot data).
#
# <device-id> and <name> mirror RETROFORGE_DEVICE_ID / RETROFORGE_DEVICE_NAME in the
# runtime profiles (the entry title must match the identity the OS reports);
# tests/test-bls.sh cross-checks the two stay in sync. Every
# <dtb> must exist under kernel/dts/qcom/ and every board DTB must be covered
# here or by the filename-derived top-dpad entry.
#
# The bootargs column carries only what is SPECIFIC to the board — the args every
# board gets (quiet, video=efifb:off, console=tty0, ...) live in BOOT_CMDLINE in
# boot/gen-bls.sh. In practice that means irqaffinity, pinned to the SoC's
# LITTLE cluster so device interrupts stay off the big cores: 0-2 on SM8550
# (3x A510), 0-1 on SM8650 (2x A520). The SM8250 rows carry no irqaffinity, so
# the kernel's default spread applies there, and their column is empty. The SM8550
# rows' allow_mismatched_32bit_el0 / fw_devlink.strict / pcie_ports are SoC
# workarounds and are deliberately absent from the SM8250 rows; so is the
# 045e:028e USB polling quirk, which only some boards carry.
# The SM6115 rows (MANGMI Air X, three panel variants of one board — the DTS
# decides the panel driver, so the user has to pick the right one — and the
# Air Y) carry what ROCKNIX's SM6115 EXTRA_CMDLINE adds beyond the common
# line: gpt, ssbd=force-off, kpti=off (Spectre-v4 / Meltdown mitigations off
# on the A73/A53 cluster, a performance choice ROCKNIX made for this SoC).
# No irqaffinity: the default IRQ spread is kept until the SM6115 tuning pass
# measures otherwise (ROCKNIX pins GPU/MDSS to cpu3 from userspace).
# iommu.strict=0 batches the SMMU TLB invalidations of DMA-API devices (SD,
# eMMC, USB, Wi-Fi, venus, QUP; the GPU and display bypass the DMA API), as
# ROCKNIX's SM6115 IOMMU_DEFAULT_DMA_LAZY does: strict mode measured 3.2 unmaps
# per received Wi-Fi packet at ~7 us each, a quarter of that the TLB sync.
# swiotlb=4096 shrinks the bounce pool from 64 MB to 8 MB: everything DMAs
# through the SMMU, and the pool's high-water mark after a 7 h session was 4 KB.
# SM8750 (Oryon 2+6) rows use irqaffinity=0-1 and nothing else: Oryon has no
# 32-bit EL0 (so no allow_mismatched), and neither board has a USB gamepad
# (so no 045e:028e). The Odin 3 row carries its stick calibration as rsinput
# module params (min/max ±1024, deadzone 70 — ROCKNIX SM8750 1300's values):
# the peer patch changes the driver's global defaults, which would recalibrate
# every rsinput board in our combined kernel; the cmdline scopes it per board.
# SM4450 (Snapdragon G1 Gen 2: 2x A78 + 6x A55) rows — the Anbernic RG 55G1 and four Retroid
# Pocket Classic revisions — carry only `gpt`, the one arg ROCKNIX's SM4450 EXTRA_CMDLINE adds
# beyond our common line. No irqaffinity until a tuning pass measures one (ROCKNIX sets none),
# and no allow_mismatched_32bit_el0: both clusters run 32-bit EL0.
anbernic-rg55g1	Anbernic RG 55G1	sm4450-anbernic-rg55g1	gpt
ayaneo-pocket-ace	AYANEO Pocket ACE	qcs8550-ayaneo-pocketace	allow_mismatched_32bit_el0 fw_devlink.strict=1 pcie_ports=compat irqaffinity=0-2 usbcore.interrupt_interval_override=045e:028e:2
ayaneo-pocket-dmg	AYANEO Pocket DMG	qcs8550-ayaneo-pocketdmg	allow_mismatched_32bit_el0 fw_devlink.strict=1 pcie_ports=compat irqaffinity=0-2 usbcore.interrupt_interval_override=045e:028e:2
